      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bear Creek meanders through Bear Valley before joining the South Platte near Englewood, linking the town to Colorado's river system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Creek_(Colorado)"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bear Valley earned Jefferson County Landmark status in 1976 and was later named a Colorado Centennial Ranch in 1987.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Creek_(Colorado)"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alexander Rooney, originally from Ohio or Iowa, arrived in 1860 chasing Colorado's gold rush and later founded the historic Rooney Ranch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Creek_(Colorado)"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2010 the Rooney family was honored in the Jefferson County Historical Commission Hall of Fame for preserving the town's pioneer heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bear_Creek_(Colorado)"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rooney Ranch once stood as Bear Valley’s largest cattle ranch, with its stone building perched above Bear Creek near today’s Bandimere Speedway.",
